# Pinned `spec` revision the conformance runner validates against.
#
# The runner refuses to run if the spec checkout it is given is not at this
# commit (override with --allow-spec-drift when deliberately testing against
# unreleased vocabulary). Without a pin the suite silently tracks whatever is
# on spec `main`, so a run that passed yesterday can pass today for a
# different reason.
#
# To re-pin: check out the new spec revision, put its full SHA and its
# VOCAB_VERSIONS line below, run `make -C . conformance` (or
# `scripts/run_conformance.py`), and record the resulting counts in the PR.

# Pinned at the MERGE commit of jayostis/spec PR #21 on `main`
# (core v3.10 / health v2.8 / clinical v1.19 / coverage v1.7; tag
# `vocab/core-v3.10` points at this commit).
#
# `repo=` MOVED, and that is deliberate rather than a typo. Every previous pin
# named the-cascade-protocol/spec; this commit is not on that repository and is
# not an ancestor of its `main`, which is still at core 3.8 / clinical 1.17 /
# coverage 1.6 and whose core.shapes.ttl contains no ConsentScopeShape. core
# v3.9 and v3.10, clinical v1.18 and v1.19, and coverage v1.7 exist today only
# on the fork. CI clones `repo=` and checks out `commit=`, so naming the org
# here would fail before a single fixture ran. Move `repo=` back to the org in
# the same commit that re-pins to an org SHA, once this vocabulary lands there.
#
# THIS PIN MOVES THREE VOCABULARIES, not one. core 3.8 -> 3.10, clinical
# 1.17 -> 1.19, coverage 1.6 -> 1.7. Two of those five version steps are
# NOT widening -- clinical v1.18 and coverage v1.7 both move records from
# unexamined to examined, so each could in principle reject a record that
# validated before. That is why the whole suite was re-run at BOTH pins and
# diffed fixture by fixture rather than only counted.
#
# WHAT MOVING THE PIN DID: exactly one verdict changed across all 163
# fixtures, and it is the one this PR exists to cause --
# clinical/social-history-consent-scope-wrong-value.INVALID.ttl goes
# NO_VIOLATION -> pass, because core v3.10's cascade:ConsentScopeShape is
# the first constraint anywhere in this specification that mentions consent.
# No existing fixture changed verdict, gained a warning or lost one.
#
#   old pin 9b13ae4 : 136 passed / 27 failed / 163 total, 63,334 checks
#   new pin 40e581f : 137 passed / 26 failed / 163 total, 63,354 checks
#
# The 26 failures are the same 26 (fixture, reason) pairs KNOWN_FAILURES.json
# already carried, so no entry is added and none is removed. Only the file's
# `specPin` scalar advances, which check_baseline.py requires and refuses to
# run without.
#
# WHERE THE +20 CONSTRAINT CHECKS WENT, since a version row that reaches no
# fixture is the thing this repository exists to catch:
#   +8   the two new consent-scope fixtures, 12 -> 16 each. Those 4 are
#        cascade:ConsentScopeShape's nodeKind / in / minCount / maxCount.
#   +12  the six coverage fixtures, 47 -> 49 each: coverage v1.7's new
#        sh:property block on coverage:sourceRecordId (datatype, maxCount).
#   +0   clinical v1.18 and v1.19. Both act on clinical:CoverageRecord --
#        v1.18 shapes the class, v1.19 adds CoverageTypeVocabularyShape --
#        and NO fixture asserts that class any more, because PR #4 retyped
#        coverage-001 to coverage:InsurancePlan. spec's own changelog says
#        so. A legacy-read fixture for it is a separate piece of work.
# health, checkup and pots are unchanged by this commit.

